course: dictionary
lesson: 13897
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You work out which one is meant by reading the words around it. This is context again. «Sam was lagging behind the others on the hill.» Lagging here is about moving more slowly and falling behind.
explain: «Dad wrapped lagging around the hot water pipes to keep the heat in.» This lagging is not a movement at all. It is a covering. The clues are wrapped, pipes and keep the heat in.
explain: «My video call keeps lagging, so my friend's voice comes out in jerky bits.» Here lagging means slow and jerky, because the connection cannot keep up. Always try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Lagging means falling behind, moving more slowly than others.
fact: Lagging is material wrapped around pipes, tanks or boilers to keep heat in and stop them freezing.
fact: A lagging game or video call is slow and jerky because the connection or computer cannot keep up.
fact: «Lagging behind» is often said about a runner at the back of a race.
fact: One word can have several meanings, so always check the clues in the sentence.
exercise: «Sam was lagging behind the rest of the class on the walk.» What does lagging mean here? | Shouting loudly | *Falling behind, moving more slowly | Covered with warm material | Glowing brightly
exercise: «Dad wrapped lagging around the hot water tank.» What is the lagging in this sentence? | A type of cloud | A game on the computer | A fast runner in a race | *A covering that keeps heat in
exercise: «The game keeps lagging, so I keep missing my shots.» What does lagging mean? | Wrapped around pipes to stop freezing | Very happy and loud | *Slow and jerky because the connection cannot keep up | Falling behind in a race
test: «Mia was lagging behind her friends on the way home.» What does lagging mean? | *Moving more slowly than the others | Shouting for help | Glowing in the dark | Covered in warm material
test: «The video call was lagging, and her voice came out in jumps.» What does lagging mean? | Very quiet | Wrapped in material to stop freezing | Falling behind with homework | *Slow and jerky because the connection cannot keep up
exam: Which meaning fits «The pipes were wrapped in lagging to stop them freezing»? | *Material that keeps heat in | Moving more slowly than others | Falling behind in a race | A slow, jerky game
